<newsitem itemid="369046" id="root" date="1997-02-11" xml:lang="en">
<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Stanbic year shr, div rises.</title>
<headline>Stanbic year shr, div rises.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Yr ended December 31</p>
<p>		(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>Shr (cts)</p>
<p>    - headline		   1,311	   vs 1,053</p>
<p>    - attrib		     1,289	   vs 1,015</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		    407	     vs 327</p>
<p>    Net income		   1,552	   vs 1,222</p>
<p>    Net interest income	3,694	   vs 3,368</p>
<p>    Other operating expenses 2,426	   vs 2,086</p>
<p>Provisions for credit losses</p>
<p>				     0.59	    vs 0.52</p>
<p>    Pre-tax			1,909	   vs 1,697</p>
<p>    Tax			    0.55	    vs 0.55</p>
<p>Div payable March 20</p>
<p>On register February 28</p>
<p>Full name: Standard Bank Investment Corp Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts polled by Reuters had forecast earnings per share of 1,300 cents, with the range a tight 1,300-1,305, and a dividend of 400 cents, with a range 390-405.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
